// The child list itself.
//
// A child is an item, which is the whole grammar: there is one syntactic form and
// everything -- container, leaf, definition call -- is spelled with it. The three
// children per container cap that idml enforces is a *checking* rule, not a
// parsing one, so it is not applied here; the loader reports it with a line
// number rather than the parser losing the fourth child.

par_ufill3(int[] pos, int[] kids) {
  while (par_is(pos, "}") = 0 && par_kind(pos) != (import lex_k_eof)) {
    int item = par_item(pos);
    push(kids, item);
  }
} return void;
